+; Lead-in tone in milliseconds (default: 0, none): a steady 1 kHz tone at the
+; level of the frame, with a ramp of 5 ms at each end, played just ahead of
+; the preamble of every frame. For a radio that keys itself on the audio
+; (VOX): it starts transmitting only after it has heard audio for its attack
+; time, and that time is otherwise taken out of the start of the preamble,
+; which the receiver acquires on. Set it to the attack time plus a margin.
+; Applies to frames sent by the broadcast and ARQ data paths.
+; Range: 0 .. 1000 (values outside are ignored).
+tx_leadin_ms = 0
